WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.980
If you had told me before I got into this

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.690
whole line of work that I'm doing,

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:07.740
that modeling was difficult
or at all arduous,

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:08.820
I would've laughed.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:09.783
Hmm

00:00:09.783 --> 00:00:10.616
I would've said, "What
are you talking about?

00:00:10.616 --> 00:00:12.600
That looks like the
easiest job in the world."

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:13.980
But Sony, you'll back me up.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:14.813
Yeah.

00:00:14.813 --> 00:00:16.140
Whenever I've had to be
part of a photo shoot.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.010
Yep.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.990
And they want me to smile and they're,

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:21.660
you know they're taking
pictures for anything, any

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:22.493
Yeah.

00:00:22.493 --> 00:00:24.090
Article or any kind of
publicity that I've been doing

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:27.033
over the 30 years that
I've been doing this,

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.350
I, there comes a point where I go "Damn."

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:32.183
Yeah

00:00:32.183 --> 00:00:33.690
"This is not fun.

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:36.120
This is not fun the way
you'd think it would be fun."

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.470
It's, there actually is,

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.040
and I can't describe why
it's difficult, but it is.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.720
I, I know, I don't know why it is either.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:45.120
I just, I've, I've been doing it so long

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.540
that it's become like
second nature for me.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:49.373
Mm hmm.

00:00:49.373 --> 00:00:51.983
And, and when I work, I've
worked other jobs in my life.

00:00:51.983 --> 00:00:52.816
Mm hmm.

00:00:52.816 --> 00:00:55.170
So, I just compare that to

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:56.296
Yes.

00:00:56.296 --> 00:00:57.129
Whatever else I've done.

00:00:57.129 --> 00:01:01.350
And, and it, and it is easier,
I have to say, than you know,

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:03.100
working a minimum wage job or

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.090
during the pandemic I went tree planting.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:07.980
So, that was super hard.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.110
Wait, what was, what do you
mean you went tree planting?

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:11.525
How's that work?

00:01:11.525 --> 00:01:12.660
It's like a job in Canada that you can do.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:16.890
You can go up north and plant
trees for 9 cents a tree.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:17.820
It's like peace work.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:20.160
I, I wanted to do
something that was kind of

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.510
outside of modeling when
everything shut down.

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:25.410
And so yeah,

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:28.210
I went up north with my best friend and

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.181
That's so funny.

00:01:30.181 --> 00:01:31.014
And we planted trees.

00:01:31.014 --> 00:01:31.980
If I had to describe what's
the opposite of modeling,

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.573
I would say agriculture.

00:01:33.573 --> 00:01:34.811
(group laughing)

00:01:34.811 --> 00:01:35.644
I really would.

00:01:35.644 --> 00:01:36.477
Yeah.

00:01:36.477 --> 00:01:37.860
I mean, I'm not even joking, but,

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.770
well, first of all that
sounds like a very, I mean,

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:44.520
2000 trees a day, is that what
you do in this tree planting?

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:45.840
Close to, yeah.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:46.740
But that was just me.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:48.300
You know, some of the boys like,

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:51.210
some of the stronger
guys would plant 4,000.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.680
Yeah. But half of those die.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:53.700
They're not being careful.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:56.310
So you'd make what, $180 a day?

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:57.143
Is that right?

00:01:57.143 --> 00:01:57.976
Yeah, close to.

00:01:57.976 --> 00:01:58.809
That's pretty good.

00:01:58.809 --> 00:01:59.642
Yeah, but the other thing is.

00:01:59.642 --> 00:02:00.475
Yeah.

00:02:00.475 --> 00:02:01.308
You're planting trees,

00:02:01.308 --> 00:02:02.891
which is such an amazing thing to do.

00:02:02.891 --> 00:02:03.724
Yeah.

00:02:03.724 --> 00:02:04.680
I mean, I, I, I think if everybody,

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.840
if they figured out a way
that everybody on earth

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.490
could plant like four trees a day.

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:09.323
Yeah.

00:02:09.323 --> 00:02:10.410
Well, then we'd have to water them,

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:11.760
and we don't have the water.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:12.780
Oh.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:13.942
Okay. This is getting grim.

00:02:13.942 --> 00:02:16.680
Well, anyway, I think it's
really great what you did.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:18.390
I think it, I think that's very cool.

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:19.223
Thank You. Yeah.

00:02:19.223 --> 00:02:21.570
I, I went a little crazy up there,

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:24.060
like because you're, you're,
you're in a piece of land

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:26.370
on your own for like eight hours a day.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:29.430
So, you know, a helicopter
would fly by every day

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:31.050
and every day I'd make the same joke.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.843
Like, Oh, there's my ride.

00:02:32.843 --> 00:02:33.676
(group laughing)

00:02:33.676 --> 00:02:35.490
And like each day it got
funnier and funnier and I

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:36.630
Wow, you guys are a lot alike.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:38.567
You know what Molly?

00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:39.960
(Conan laughing)

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:41.100
you're my, you're,

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.330
you're my kind of person.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:43.163
Yeah.

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:45.720
You, you are a tall thin
redhead that loves to

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.760
make the same joke over
and over and over again

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.026
until it becomes funny only to you.

00:02:50.026 --> 00:02:50.859
(group laughing)

00:02:50.859 --> 00:02:53.040
God bless you, Molly.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:54.363
You're my new hero.

